B.a3I=new A.a0("How do I add my parents or children?","Go to Me \u2192 Family & consent \u2192 Add family member. Adults then give their consent (in person, or you declare you are their caregiver); for children under 18 you give guardian consent. Until then their health details stay locked.")
B.a2F=new A.a0("Why is there a \ud83d\udd12 next to a family member?","Their consent hasn't been recorded yet. India's data protection law (DPDP Act) means we can't store their health details until they \u2014 or a guardian for children \u2014 agree. Tap their name to record consent.")
B.a2J=new A.a0("How do medicine reminders work?","Add a medicine with its times in Home \u2192 Medications and tick each dose. On the phone app, the phone rings at dose time even when the app is closed. Open the app at least once a week so the alarms stay set.")
B.a2M=new A.a0("How do I send a report to my doctor?",'Open the Health vault, tap the record, then "Share securely". Choose 1 hour, 24 hours or 7 days and send the link on WhatsApp. The link stops working after that time.')
B.a2V=new A.a0("Who can see my health records?","Only your family account. Doctors see a record only through a link you share, until it expires. When SOS launches, the medic will see the emergency profile only during an active SOS.")
B.a3y=new A.a0("My society approval is still pending","Your RWA (society office) checks your proof of residence. If it takes more than 2 days, please ask them, or write to us below.")
B.a3_=new A.a0("Is SOS available yet?","PulseGrid SOS is being set up with medics in partner societies. Until it is switched on for your society, please call 112 (emergency) or 108 (ambulance) directly.")
B.a2Y=new A.a0("How do I download or delete my data?",'Me \u2192 Privacy & my data. "Download a copy" saves everything we store; "Delete my account" erases it all permanently.')
